# THE 1.2.0 SHAPE AGAINST ONE WORKED EXAMPLE OF EACH LIFT (plan 8.1e item 5;
# the lifts are plan 2.19). Written 2026-10-20, before any lift past the first is
# built, so the shape is tested before data arrives, not fitted to it after.
#
# Each example is a real verse, real records and the structure layer's own
# parts. Everything in claim:, bor: and bos: must be declared
# (tests/test_lift_shapes.py checks it). The first version found five gaps
# (docs/review/lift-shapes-1.2.0.md) and wrote them in a gap: namespace; Doug
# approved each on the refreshed 1.2.0 inventory (2026-10-20), so they are now
# the vocabulary's own terms: bor:spoke_to (G1), claim:modality_foretold (G2),
# claim:evidencedBy reaching a phrase or a turn (G4), parts of the structure
# addressed with the verse pages' book codes (G5), a described statement
# labelled by its plain form (G6).
#
# A claim's triple is stated (inside its voice's graph, at the end) only when
# the statement is made outright. A command, a promise, a prediction, a
# negated clause or a verb whose form does not say it happened is described
# and never stated.

@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix claim: <https://bibleontology.org/ns/claim#> .
@prefix bor:   <https://bibleontology.org/ns/relation#> .
@prefix bos:   <https://bibleontology.org/ns/structure#> .
@prefix e:     <https://bibleontology.org/e/> .
@prefix p:     <https://bibleontology.org/p/> .
@prefix voice: <https://bibleontology.org/voice/> .
@prefix x:     <https://bibleontology.org/claim/example-> .

# ---- 1. A verb statement (lift 1, built): John 3:16 ------------------------
x:verb a claim:Claim ;
    claim:subject e:god ; claim:relation bor:states ; claim:object e:world ;
    claim:verse p:John.3.16 ; claim:certainty claim:explicit ;
    claim:verbLabel "loved" ; claim:mood "indicative" ; claim:person "third" ;
    claim:negated false ;
    claim:modality claim:modality_stated ; claim:modalityFrom "form" ;
    claim:family claim:family_verb_emotion ;
    claim:clause <https://bibleontology.org/structure/John.3.16#cl0> ;
    claim:voice claim:narrator .

# ---- 2. A place (lift 2): Gen 13:3, "to Bethel" -----------------------------
# The hand row stays the curated form; the lift is its evidence: the
# prepositional phrase, by its word in the structure (G4).
x:place a claim:Claim ;
    claim:subject e:abraham ; claim:relation bor:traveled_to ; claim:object e:beth_el ;
    claim:verse p:Gen.13.3 ; claim:certainty claim:explicit ;
    claim:evidencedBy <https://bibleontology.org/structure/Gen.13.3#w13> ;
    claim:voice claim:narrator .

# ---- 3. Who speaks to whom (lift 3): Gen 22:7, "Isaac said to Abraham" -------
# The narrator's statement, the speech TURN its evidence (G1, G4).
x:speech a claim:Claim ;
    claim:subject e:isaac ; claim:relation bor:spoke_to ; claim:object e:abraham ;
    claim:verse p:Gen.22.7 ; claim:certainty claim:explicit ;
    claim:evidencedBy <https://bibleontology.org/structure/Gen.22.7#turn0> ;
    claim:voice claim:narrator .

# ---- 4. A command (lift 4): Deut 6:5, "you shall love the LORD your God" ----
# Moses' words to Israel. The form is a weqatal, which does not decide it;
# a reading says "commanded", and modalityFrom says so. Its label is the
# verb's plain form (G6): nothing happened. Described, NEVER stated.
x:command a claim:Claim ;
    claim:subject e:children_of_israel ; claim:relation bor:states ; claim:object e:god ;
    claim:verse p:Deut.6.5 ; claim:certainty claim:explicit ;
    claim:verbLabel "love" ; claim:mood "weqatal" ; claim:stem "qal" ; claim:person "second" ;
    claim:negated false ;
    claim:modality claim:modality_commanded ; claim:modalityFrom "reading" ;
    claim:family claim:family_verb_emotion ;
    claim:clause <https://bibleontology.org/structure/Deut.6.5#cl0> ;
    claim:claimedBy e:moses ;
    claim:voice voice:moses .

# ...and a prediction of another (G2): John 13:38, "the rooster will not crow
# until you have denied Me three times" (Jesus to Peter). Described, never
# stated: that it came true is Mark 14:72's statement, the narrator's.
x:foretold a claim:Claim ;
    claim:subject e:peter ; claim:relation bor:states ; claim:object e:jesus ;
    claim:verse p:John.13.38 ; claim:certainty claim:explicit ;
    claim:verbLabel "deny" ; claim:mood "subjunctive" ; claim:negated false ;
    claim:modality claim:modality_foretold ; claim:modalityFrom "reading" ;
    claim:claimedBy e:jesus ;
    claim:voice voice:jesus .

# ---- 5. A reason between statements (lift 5): John 3:16 ----------------------
# "God so loved the world THAT he gave his one and only Son": the structure
# links cl0 to cl1 with bos:result. No claim term is needed: the two claims
# meet through claim:clause, at the address the structure layer will use (G5).
x:reason-given a claim:Claim ;
    claim:subject e:god ; claim:relation bor:states ; claim:object e:jesus ;
    claim:verse p:John.3.16 ; claim:certainty claim:explicit ;
    claim:verbLabel "gave" ; claim:mood "indicative" ; claim:negated false ;
    claim:modality claim:modality_stated ; claim:modalityFrom "form" ;
    claim:clause <https://bibleontology.org/structure/John.3.16#cl1> ;
    claim:voice claim:narrator .
<https://bibleontology.org/structure/John.3.16#cl0> a bos:Clause ;
    bos:result <https://bibleontology.org/structure/John.3.16#cl1> .
<https://bibleontology.org/structure/John.3.16#cl1> a bos:Clause .

# ---- 6. Identity (lift 6): John 6:35, "I am the bread of life" ---------------
# The hand row (titled) is the narrator's; the clause is in Jesus' turn. Whose
# words it is, the structure's turn says (sender).
x:identity a claim:Claim ;
    claim:subject e:jesus ; claim:relation bor:titled ; claim:object e:the_bread_of_life ;
    claim:verse p:John.6.35 ; claim:certainty claim:explicit ;
    claim:evidencedBy <https://bibleontology.org/structure/John.6.35#cl1> ;
    claim:voice claim:narrator .

# ---- 7. Family from apposition (lift 6): 1 Sam 10:21, "Saul son of Kish" -----
# The apposition is inside cl2 ("Saul the son of Kish was taken"), evidence for
# the hand row from a verse it did not yet cite (G4).
x:family a claim:Claim ;
    claim:subject e:kish ; claim:relation bor:father_of ; claim:object e:saul ;
    claim:verse p:1Chr.8.33, p:1Sam.9.1, p:1Sam.14.51, p:1Sam.10.21 ; claim:certainty claim:explicit ;
    claim:evidencedBy <https://bibleontology.org/structure/1Sam.10.21#cl2> ;
    claim:voice claim:narrator .

# ---- What is STATED: only the statements made outright ----------------------
# never a bor:states triple (plan 8.3f, Doug 2026-10-22, "states: A"): the
# relation has no verb, so different sentences would share one triple; a verb
# statement is described by its claim, verb and all, and stated nowhere
claim:narrator {
    e:abraham bor:traveled_to e:beth_el .
    e:isaac bor:spoke_to e:abraham .
    e:jesus bor:titled e:the_bread_of_life .
    e:kish bor:father_of e:saul .
}
voice:moses {
}
voice:jesus {
}
